    <h2>Working on Springfield's older homes</h2>
    <p>A lot of our Springfield work is in the houses around downtown and the historic district, many built before 1940. Knob-and-tube wiring, two-prong outlets and 60-amp fuse boxes are still common, and we have rewired dozens of these homes without losing their plaster or their character.</p>
    <h2>Permits and inspections</h2>
    <p>We pull permits through the city's building department every week and know what its inspectors look for, which keeps panel swaps and rewires on schedule.</p>
    <h2>Newer neighborhoods</h2>
    <p>On the newer west side, the calls are different: EV chargers, panel capacity for heat pumps, and recessed lighting in basements being finished.</p>
